IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Part III, Division 2 (Microchipping)
-- and Division 3 (Changes to recorded information)
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of ss. 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26A, 26B, 26C (Division 2,
-- "Microchipping") and s. 26D (Division 3, "Changes to recorded
-- information"), as at the compilation dated 28 Nov 2024 [version
-- 08-b0-00], re-verified current 2026-09-09. Source: lines 641-709 of the
-- verbatim compilation
-- (canon/subjects/western-australia/dog-act-1976/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47983.txt).
-- Shared s. 3 definitions this file reads (DogProfile, Penalty) live in
-- dog-act-domain.l4, imported above.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site with @ref, never expanded):
--   * s. 14(3) (prescribed particulars recorded on the local government's
--     register) -- read by s. 26D(a); outside this chunk's line range.
--   * s. 22(1) "the relevant day" -- defined by reference to the day the
--     Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 21 came into operation, a fact outside
--     this excerpt; recorded as a bare fact-supplied BOOLEAN.
--   * s. 33F(1), s. 33F generally, s. 33F(6)(a), s. 33I(1)(a)(i)/(d) and
--     s. 33I(1)(b) -- all read by s. 22(3)'s dangerous-dog-(declared)
--     grace periods. These ARE encoded elsewhere in this corpus
--     (dog-act-1976.l4, Part VI Division 2), by a parallel chunk of this
--     same workflow, but per that workflow's rules this file does not
--     IMPORT that module -- each s. 22(3)(a)-(d) period is a bare
--     fact-supplied BOOLEAN here, cited at its site.
--
-- One ambiguity was found and materialised as a design choice below
-- (F-S21-DANGEROUS-DOG-SCOPE, at s. 21's offence predicates).
-- =============================================================================

§ `Shared penalty preset for this module`

-- The recurring flat "Penalty: a fine of $5 000" shape, with no minimum, no
-- imprisonment and no further-offence add-on: ss. 21(1), 21(2), 23(1), 24,
-- 25, 26A, 26B(1), 26C, 26D.
`the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty (flat $5,000)` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

§ `Part III, Division 2 -- Microchipping`
§§ `21. Microchipping of dogs other than dangerous dogs`

-- AMBIGUITY (F-S21-DANGEROUS-DOG-SCOPE): s. 21's HEADING reads "Microchipping
-- of dogs other than dangerous dogs", but s. 21(1)-(2)'s OPERATIVE text is
-- not textually limited to non-dangerous dogs -- it reads "the owner of a
-- dog must ensure...". Two readings: (A) the heading is descriptive/
-- historical only, and s. 21(1)-(2) applies to EVERY dog, dangerous or not,
-- running concurrently with s. 22's dangerous-dog-specific duty (which
-- carries a materially higher penalty and its own exemption/grace-period
-- mechanics); or (B) the heading substantively confines s. 21 to
-- non-dangerous dogs, so a dangerous dog is governed exclusively by s. 22.
-- Taken: reading (A) -- the operative words control over the heading, and
-- this is corroborated by s. 22(6) itself ("Nothing in subsection (3)
-- affects the operation of section 21(1) or (2) in relation to a
-- particular dog"), which presupposes that s. 21(1)/(2) DOES keep
-- operating for a dog that is within s. 22(3)'s grace-period scope -- a
-- presupposition reading (B) would make redundant. (Registration-refusal
-- grounds elsewhere in this Act, ss. 16(3)(da) and 17A(2)(d) -- outside
-- this chunk -- also list "required under section 21 or 22" as two
-- independent bases, neither displacing the other, which is consistent
-- with (A).) Rejected: reading (B). No dog-type gate is therefore added to
-- the s. 21 predicates below; s. 22's dog-type gate is separate and
-- additional, not a substitute.
DECLARE `S21(1) Facts` HAS
    `on or after 1 November 2013`                                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog has reached 3 months of age`                                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is registered under this Act, or under the law of another State or a Territory, so that its registration was in effect on 31 October 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is microchipped`                                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Microchipping Exemption Facts` HAS
    `a certificate given by a veterinarian, stating that implantation of a microchip in the dog may adversely affect the dog's health and welfare, applies in respect of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is under 3 months of age`                                                                                                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 21(4)-(5), s. 22(4)-(5)
-- s. 21(4)-(5) and s. 22(4)-(5) are verbatim identical -- one shared test.
GIVEN f IS A `Microchipping Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is exempt from microchipping` f MEANS
        f's `a certificate given by a veterinarian, stating that implantation of a microchip in the dog may adversely affect the dog's health and welfare, applies in respect of the dog`
    AND NOT f's `dog is under 3 months of age`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 21(1), (3)
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
GIVEN facts IS A `S21(1) Facts`, exemption IS A `Microchipping Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) offence -- dog not microchipped (pre-Nov-2013-registration limb)` facts exemption MEANS
        facts's `on or after 1 November 2013`
    AND facts's `dog has reached 3 months of age`
    AND NOT facts's `dog is registered under this Act, or under the law of another State or a Territory, so that its registration was in effect on 31 October 2013`
    AND NOT facts's `dog is microchipped`
    AND NOT `the dog is exempt from microchipping` exemption

DECLARE `S21(2) Facts` HAS
    `on or after 1 November 2015`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is microchipped`             IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 21(2)-(3)
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
GIVEN facts IS A `S21(2) Facts`, exemption IS A `Microchipping Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) offence -- dog not microchipped (general duty from 1 November 2015)` facts exemption MEANS
        facts's `on or after 1 November 2015`
    AND facts's `dog has reached 3 months of age`
    AND NOT facts's `dog is microchipped`
    AND NOT `the dog is exempt from microchipping` exemption

§§ `22. Microchipping of dangerous dogs`

DECLARE `S22 Facts` HAS
    `after the relevant day`          IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 22(1) "relevant day" -- scoped out, fact-supplied (30 days after the Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 21 commencement date, a fact outside this excerpt)
    `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is microchipped`             IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `S22(3) Grace Period Facts` HAS
    `within the 7-day period after the giving of the s 33F(1) notice declaring the dog a dangerous dog (declared)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 33F(1) -- scoped out, fact-supplied (encoded in dog-act-1976.l4, not imported)
    `within the period beginning when the owner lodges an objection under s 33F or applies for review under s 33I(1)(b), and ending 7 days after the determination of that objection or review` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss. 33F, 33I(1)(b) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `within the 7-day period after the giving of a s 33F(6)(a) notice as to the dismissal of an objection`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 33F(6)(a) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `within the period beginning when the owner applies for a review under s 33I(1)(a)(i) or (d), and ending 7 days after the determination of that review`      IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 33I(1)(a)(i), (d) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 22(3)
GIVEN g IS A `S22(3) Grace Period Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 22(3) grace period currently applies to the dog` g MEANS
        g's `within the 7-day period after the giving of the s 33F(1) notice declaring the dog a dangerous dog (declared)`
    OR  g's `within the period beginning when the owner lodges an objection under s 33F or applies for review under s 33I(1)(b), and ending 7 days after the determination of that objection or review`
    OR  g's `within the 7-day period after the giving of a s 33F(6)(a) notice as to the dismissal of an objection`
    OR  g's `within the period beginning when the owner applies for a review under s 33I(1)(a)(i) or (d), and ending 7 days after the determination of that review`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 22(2)-(3)
-- Penalty: (a) a fine of $10,000, minimum $500; (b) $500 for each separate
-- and further offence under the Interpretation Act 1984 s. 71 (not
-- computed -- see dog-act-domain.l4's Penalty record).
--
-- s. 22(3)'s grace period is textually confined to "a dangerous dog
-- (declared)" -- so it is gated here on DogProfile's own s. 33E(1)-declared
-- flag, not on the broader `the dog is a dangerous dog` test used for the
-- offence gate itself. A dangerous dog (restricted breed) or a commercial
-- security dog gets no grace period under s. 22(3), even though both are
-- "dangerous dogs" for the offence gate.
GIVEN dog IS A DogProfile, facts IS A `S22 Facts`, exemption IS A `Microchipping Exemption Facts`, grace IS A `S22(3) Grace Period Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) offence -- dangerous dog not microchipped` dog facts exemption grace MEANS
        `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog
    AND facts's `after the relevant day`
    AND facts's `dog has reached 3 months of age`
    AND NOT facts's `dog is microchipped`
    AND NOT `the dog is exempt from microchipping` exemption
    AND NOT (   dog's `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)`
             AND `a s 22(3) grace period currently applies to the dog` grace)

`s 22(2) penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS JUST 500, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS JUST 500

-- s. 22(6): confirmed by design above -- the s. 21(1)/(2) offence predicates
-- above never read `grace`, so a s. 22(3) grace period can never excuse
-- non-compliance with s. 21(1) or (2) for the same dog. (This is what makes
-- s. 22(6) a non-vacuous provision under the F-S21-DANGEROUS-DOG-SCOPE
-- taken reading above.)

§§ `23. Notice to be given of microchip information`

DECLARE `Microchipping Act Party` IS ONE OF
    `Dog Owner`
    `Microchip Implanter`
    `Person Who Effected The Transfer`

DECLARE `Microchipping Act Action` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of microchip information to the local government`
    `give notice of prescribed information to the microchip database company`
    `give notice of transfer information to the microchip database company`
    `give notice of a change to registration information to the local government`
    `give notice of a change to microchip database information to the microchip database company`

DECLARE `S23 Notice` HAS
    `states the name of the microchip database company for the dog`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the microchip's unique identification number for the dog` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 23(1)
GIVEN n IS A `S23 Notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 23(1) notice satisfies its content requirements` n MEANS
        n's `states the name of the microchip database company for the dog`
    AND n's `states the microchip's unique identification number for the dog`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 23(1)-(2)
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
-- s. 23(2): the duty below does not arise at all if the microchip
-- information has been, or will be, provided with a registration
-- application -- modelled as a gate rather than a further deontic branch,
-- following the "mandatory vs discretionary" IF/ELSE FULFILLED pattern.
GIVEN `information was, or will be, provided with an application to the local government to register the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Microchipping Act Party` `Microchipping Act Action`
`s 23(1) notification duty` `information was, or will be, provided with an application to the local government to register the dog` MEANS
    IF `information was, or will be, provided with an application to the local government to register the dog`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE
        PARTY  `Dog Owner`
        MUST   `give notice of microchip information to the local government`
        WITHIN 7
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH BY `Dog Owner`
               BECAUSE "the local government of the district where the dog is ordinarily kept or ordinarily permitted to live was not given notice of the microchip database company and the microchip's unique identification number within 7 days of the microchipping, as s 23(1) requires"

§§ `24. Microchip implanter to give information to microchip database company`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 24
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
`s 24 notification duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `Microchip Implanter`
    MUST   `give notice of prescribed information to the microchip database company`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `Microchip Implanter`
           BECAUSE "the microchip database company for the dog was not given the prescribed information, in the form (if any) prescribed, within 7 days after the microchip was implanted, as s 24 requires"

§§ `25. Microchip database company's obligations`

DECLARE `Microchip Database Company Facts` HAS
    `information prescribed under s 24 has been given to the company in respect of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `company keeps and maintains that information in its microchip database`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 25
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
GIVEN f IS A `Microchip Database Company Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25 offence -- microchip database company fails to keep and maintain prescribed information` f MEANS
        f's `information prescribed under s 24 has been given to the company in respect of the dog`
    AND NOT f's `company keeps and maintains that information in its microchip database`

§§ `26A. Interference with microchips`

DECLARE `Microchip Interference Facts` HAS
    `person removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `person had a reasonable excuse`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 26A
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
GIVEN f IS A `Microchip Interference Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26A offence -- interference with a microchip without reasonable excuse` f MEANS
        f's `person removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a dog`
    AND NOT f's `person had a reasonable excuse`

§§ `26B. Transfer of ownership of unmicrochipped dogs`

DECLARE `Unmicrochipped Dog Transfer Facts` HAS
    `ownership of the dog was transferred`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is not microchipped`                                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time of the transfer, the person is satisfied that a certificate referred to in s 21(4) or 22(4) applies in respect of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 26B(1)-(2)
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
-- s. 26B(2): this offence applies regardless of when or whether the dog was
-- ever registered -- no registration-history field is read below, by
-- design.
GIVEN f IS A `Unmicrochipped Dog Transfer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26B(1) offence -- transferring an unmicrochipped dog without a satisfied exemption certificate` f MEANS
        f's `ownership of the dog was transferred`
    AND f's `dog is not microchipped`
    AND NOT f's `at the time of the transfer, the person is satisfied that a certificate referred to in s 21(4) or 22(4) applies in respect of the dog`

§§ `26C. Transfer of ownership of microchipped dogs`

DECLARE `S26C Notice` HAS
    `states the name and address of the person to whom ownership of the dog was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states any other changes to the information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 26C
GIVEN n IS A `S26C Notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 26C notice satisfies its content requirements` n MEANS
        n's `states the name and address of the person to whom ownership of the dog was transferred`
    AND n's `states any other changes to the information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 26C
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above).
`s 26C notification duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `Person Who Effected The Transfer`
    MUST   `give notice of transfer information to the microchip database company`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `Person Who Effected The Transfer`
           BECAUSE "the microchip database company for the dog was not given notice of the transfer within 7 days after the transfer of ownership, as s 26C requires"

§ `Part III, Division 3 -- Changes to recorded information`
§§ `26D. Notice to be given of changes to recorded information`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 26D(a)
-- Penalty: a fine of $5,000 (see `the standard microchipping/notice offence penalty` above), shared with limb (b) below.
-- s. 14(3) (prescribed particulars recorded on the local government's
-- register) is outside this chunk's assigned line range; scoped out as a
-- fact-supplied trigger.
GIVEN `there is a change to information prescribed under s 14(3) in respect of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Microchipping Act Party` `Microchipping Act Action`
`s 26D(a) notification duty -- change to registration information` `there is a change to information prescribed under s 14(3) in respect of the dog` MEANS
    IF `there is a change to information prescribed under s 14(3) in respect of the dog`
    THEN
        PARTY  `Dog Owner`
        MUST   `give notice of a change to registration information to the local government`
        WITHIN 7
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH BY `Dog Owner`
               BECAUSE "the local government with which the dog is registered was not given notice of the change to registration information within 7 days after the change, as s 26D requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 26D(b)
GIVEN `there is a change to information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Microchipping Act Party` `Microchipping Act Action`
`s 26D(b) notification duty -- change to microchip database information` `there is a change to information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog` MEANS
    IF `there is a change to information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog`
    THEN
        PARTY  `Dog Owner`
        MUST   `give notice of a change to microchip database information to the microchip database company`
        WITHIN 7
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH BY `Dog Owner`
               BECAUSE "the microchip database company for the dog was not given notice of the change to microchip database information within 7 days after the change, as s 26D requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

`a valid vet exemption certificate for an eligible dog` MEANS `Microchipping Exemption Facts` WITH
    `a certificate given by a veterinarian, stating that implantation of a microchip in the dog may adversely affect the dog's health and welfare, applies in respect of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `dog is under 3 months of age` IS FALSE

`a vet certificate for a dog under 3 months of age` MEANS `Microchipping Exemption Facts` WITH
    `a certificate given by a veterinarian, stating that implantation of a microchip in the dog may adversely affect the dog's health and welfare, applies in respect of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `dog is under 3 months of age` IS TRUE

`no vet certificate at all` MEANS `Microchipping Exemption Facts` WITH
    `a certificate given by a veterinarian, stating that implantation of a microchip in the dog may adversely affect the dog's health and welfare, applies in respect of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `dog is under 3 months of age` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the dog is exempt from microchipping` `a valid vet exemption certificate for an eligible dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is exempt from microchipping` `a vet certificate for a dog under 3 months of age`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is exempt from microchipping` `no vet certificate at all`)

`an unregistered, unchipped 4-month-old dog on 1 Dec 2013` MEANS `S21(1) Facts` WITH
    `on or after 1 November 2013` IS TRUE
    , `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS TRUE
    , `dog is registered under this Act, or under the law of another State or a Territory, so that its registration was in effect on 31 October 2013` IS FALSE
    , `dog is microchipped` IS FALSE

`a dog already registered as at 31 October 2013` MEANS `S21(1) Facts` WITH
    `on or after 1 November 2013` IS TRUE
    , `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS TRUE
    , `dog is registered under this Act, or under the law of another State or a Territory, so that its registration was in effect on 31 October 2013` IS TRUE
    , `dog is microchipped` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 21(1) offence -- dog not microchipped (pre-Nov-2013-registration limb)` `an unregistered, unchipped 4-month-old dog on 1 Dec 2013` `no vet certificate at all`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21(1) offence -- dog not microchipped (pre-Nov-2013-registration limb)` `a dog already registered as at 31 October 2013` `no vet certificate at all`)

`a 4-month-old unchipped dog on 1 Dec 2015` MEANS `S21(2) Facts` WITH
    `on or after 1 November 2015` IS TRUE
    , `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS TRUE
    , `dog is microchipped` IS FALSE

`a 4-month-old chipped dog on 1 Dec 2015` MEANS `S21(2) Facts` WITH
    `on or after 1 November 2015` IS TRUE
    , `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS TRUE
    , `dog is microchipped` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 21(2) offence -- dog not microchipped (general duty from 1 November 2015)` `a 4-month-old unchipped dog on 1 Dec 2015` `no vet certificate at all`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21(2) offence -- dog not microchipped (general duty from 1 November 2015)` `a 4-month-old chipped dog on 1 Dec 2015` `no vet certificate at all`)

`within the s 33F(1) notice's 7-day grace window` MEANS `S22(3) Grace Period Facts` WITH
    `within the 7-day period after the giving of the s 33F(1) notice declaring the dog a dangerous dog (declared)` IS TRUE
    , `within the period beginning when the owner lodges an objection under s 33F or applies for review under s 33I(1)(b), and ending 7 days after the determination of that objection or review` IS FALSE
    , `within the 7-day period after the giving of a s 33F(6)(a) notice as to the dismissal of an objection` IS FALSE
    , `within the period beginning when the owner applies for a review under s 33I(1)(a)(i) or (d), and ending 7 days after the determination of that review` IS FALSE

`no grace period currently applies` MEANS `S22(3) Grace Period Facts` WITH
    `within the 7-day period after the giving of the s 33F(1) notice declaring the dog a dangerous dog (declared)` IS FALSE
    , `within the period beginning when the owner lodges an objection under s 33F or applies for review under s 33I(1)(b), and ending 7 days after the determination of that objection or review` IS FALSE
    , `within the 7-day period after the giving of a s 33F(6)(a) notice as to the dismissal of an objection` IS FALSE
    , `within the period beginning when the owner applies for a review under s 33I(1)(a)(i) or (d), and ending 7 days after the determination of that review` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a s 22(3) grace period currently applies to the dog` `within the s 33F(1) notice's 7-day grace window`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 22(3) grace period currently applies to the dog` `no grace period currently applies`)

`a s 33E(1)-declared dangerous dog` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS TRUE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS FALSE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

`a restricted-breed dangerous dog (not declared)` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS FALSE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS TRUE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

`a non-dangerous dog` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS FALSE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS FALSE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

`a declared dangerous dog past the relevant day, unchipped` MEANS `S22 Facts` WITH
    `after the relevant day` IS TRUE
    , `dog has reached 3 months of age` IS TRUE
    , `dog is microchipped` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 22(2) offence -- dangerous dog not microchipped` `a s 33E(1)-declared dangerous dog` `a declared dangerous dog past the relevant day, unchipped` `no vet certificate at all` `no grace period currently applies`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22(2) offence -- dangerous dog not microchipped` `a s 33E(1)-declared dangerous dog` `a declared dangerous dog past the relevant day, unchipped` `no vet certificate at all` `within the s 33F(1) notice's 7-day grace window`)
-- The s 22(3) grace period does not exempt a restricted-breed dangerous dog
-- (it speaks only of "a dangerous dog (declared)"):
#ASSERT `s 22(2) offence -- dangerous dog not microchipped` `a restricted-breed dangerous dog (not declared)` `a declared dangerous dog past the relevant day, unchipped` `no vet certificate at all` `within the s 33F(1) notice's 7-day grace window`
-- A non-dangerous dog is never within s 22(2)'s gate at all:
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22(2) offence -- dangerous dog not microchipped` `a non-dangerous dog` `a declared dangerous dog past the relevant day, unchipped` `no vet certificate at all` `no grace period currently applies`)

`a complete s 23(1) notice` MEANS `S23 Notice` WITH
    `states the name of the microchip database company for the dog` IS TRUE
    , `states the microchip's unique identification number for the dog` IS TRUE

`an incomplete s 23(1) notice, missing the ID number` MEANS `S23 Notice` WITH
    `states the name of the microchip database company for the dog` IS TRUE
    , `states the microchip's unique identification number for the dog` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 23(1) notice satisfies its content requirements` `a complete s 23(1) notice`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 23(1) notice satisfies its content requirements` `an incomplete s 23(1) notice, missing the ID number`)

#TRACE `s 23(1) notification duty` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Dog Owner` DOES `give notice of microchip information to the local government` AT 5
-- Result: FULFILLED (notified within the 7-day window)

#TRACE `s 23(1) notification duty` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- no notice within 7 days of the microchipping

#TRACE `s 23(1) notification duty` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)
-- Result: FULFILLED -- s 23(2): the microchip information was already/will
-- be provided with the registration application, so the s 23(1) duty never
-- arises, regardless of elapsed time.

`info given, kept and maintained` MEANS `Microchip Database Company Facts` WITH
    `information prescribed under s 24 has been given to the company in respect of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `company keeps and maintains that information in its microchip database` IS TRUE

`info given, not kept` MEANS `Microchip Database Company Facts` WITH
    `information prescribed under s 24 has been given to the company in respect of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `company keeps and maintains that information in its microchip database` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`s 25 offence -- microchip database company fails to keep and maintain prescribed information` `info given, kept and maintained`)
#ASSERT `s 25 offence -- microchip database company fails to keep and maintain prescribed information` `info given, not kept`

#TRACE `s 24 notification duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Microchip Implanter` DOES `give notice of prescribed information to the microchip database company` AT 6
-- Result: FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 24 notification duty` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- no notice within 7 days after the microchip was implanted

`interference without excuse` MEANS `Microchip Interference Facts` WITH
    `person removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a dog` IS TRUE
    , `person had a reasonable excuse` IS FALSE

`interference with a reasonable excuse` MEANS `Microchip Interference Facts` WITH
    `person removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a dog` IS TRUE
    , `person had a reasonable excuse` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 26A offence -- interference with a microchip without reasonable excuse` `interference without excuse`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26A offence -- interference with a microchip without reasonable excuse` `interference with a reasonable excuse`)

`transfer of an unchipped dog, no satisfied exemption certificate` MEANS `Unmicrochipped Dog Transfer Facts` WITH
    `ownership of the dog was transferred` IS TRUE
    , `dog is not microchipped` IS TRUE
    , `at the time of the transfer, the person is satisfied that a certificate referred to in s 21(4) or 22(4) applies in respect of the dog` IS FALSE

`transfer of an unchipped dog, with a satisfied exemption certificate` MEANS `Unmicrochipped Dog Transfer Facts` WITH
    `ownership of the dog was transferred` IS TRUE
    , `dog is not microchipped` IS TRUE
    , `at the time of the transfer, the person is satisfied that a certificate referred to in s 21(4) or 22(4) applies in respect of the dog` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 26B(1) offence -- transferring an unmicrochipped dog without a satisfied exemption certificate` `transfer of an unchipped dog, no satisfied exemption certificate`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26B(1) offence -- transferring an unmicrochipped dog without a satisfied exemption certificate` `transfer of an unchipped dog, with a satisfied exemption certificate`)

`a complete s 26C notice` MEANS `S26C Notice` WITH
    `states the name and address of the person to whom ownership of the dog was transferred` IS TRUE
    , `states any other changes to the information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog` IS TRUE

`an incomplete s 26C notice, missing the transferee's address` MEANS `S26C Notice` WITH
    `states the name and address of the person to whom ownership of the dog was transferred` IS FALSE
    , `states any other changes to the information prescribed under s 24 in respect of the dog` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the s 26C notice satisfies its content requirements` `a complete s 26C notice`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 26C notice satisfies its content requirements` `an incomplete s 26C notice, missing the transferee's address`)

#TRACE `s 26C notification duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Person Who Effected The Transfer` DOES `give notice of transfer information to the microchip database company` AT 3
-- Result: FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 26C notification duty` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 9)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- no notice within 7 days of the transfer

#TRACE `s 26D(a) notification duty -- change to registration information` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Dog Owner` DOES `give notice of a change to registration information to the local government` AT 4
-- Result: FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 26D(a) notification duty -- change to registration information` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)
-- Result: FULFILLED -- no change to the s 14(3) information, so no duty arises

#TRACE `s 26D(b) notification duty -- change to microchip database information` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Dog Owner` DOES `give notice of a change to microchip database information to the microchip database company` AT 4
-- Result: FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 26D(b) notification duty -- change to microchip database information` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)
-- Result: FULFILLED -- no change to the s 24 information, so no duty arises
